WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.129
A data set only matters when something reads it.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:08.012
This video uses a live and an imported data set in the Report

00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:13.460
Builder and in a data pipeline, and shows the permissions that decide who can pick them.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.865
A connected data set shows up wherever you pick a data source:

00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:26.510
in the Report Builder, and in the Read a data source step of a data pipeline.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.988
Live data sets are listed under Connected data, live.

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:34.464
Imported ones are under Connected data, imported.

00:00:34.464 --> 00:00:37.560
Each is shown with the connection it reads.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.701
A report on a live data set reads the other system when it runs.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:46.778
A report on an imported data set reads the last copy, so it

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:50.290
stays fast, and it works while the source is down.

00:00:54.486 --> 00:00:59.259
In Reports, Report Builder, click New Report, then Add data set.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:04.919
Next to Content items and Users, the groups now include Connected data, live,

00:01:04.919 --> 00:01:07.306
and Connected data, imported.

00:01:07.757 --> 00:01:11.528
Under live, there are the Orders and Customers data sets.

00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:15.001
Add Orders, and its fields appear in the Data panel:

00:01:15.001 --> 00:01:16.977
the ones you chose to show.

00:01:17.428 --> 00:01:21.337
Drag Region into the columns, then the number of rows.

00:01:21.337 --> 00:01:26.548
The preview reads the API live, and shows how many orders each region has.

00:01:31.553 --> 00:01:34.119
An imported data set works the same way.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:38.136
Its card says when its copy was imported, because that is the data

00:01:38.136 --> 00:01:39.643
the report will read.

00:01:43.839 --> 00:01:48.556
In Tools, Data Pipelines, click Add Pipeline and give it a name.

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:51.589
The designer opens, ready for a source.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.211
Choose Read a data source.

00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:59.028
The same list opens, with the same groups, so a pipeline can read

00:01:59.028 --> 00:02:01.810
a live data set or an imported one.

00:02:02.261 --> 00:02:03.914
Pick Imported orders.

00:02:03.914 --> 00:02:08.140
The step now reads the copy, and the steps after it can filter,

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.161
group and send the rows on.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:19.346
Only people who can read a data set see it in a report or a pipeline.

00:02:19.346 --> 00:02:25.120
In Access Control, Roles, open a role and look for Read every connected data set.

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:28.066
Or give a role just one data set:

00:02:28.066 --> 00:02:32.290
tick Read the connected data set, with that data set's name.

00:02:32.741 --> 00:02:36.996
The rule is the same for live and imported data sets, so importing

00:02:36.996 --> 00:02:39.419
data never shows it to more people.

00:02:39.419 --> 00:02:43.201
Without the permission, the data set is not listed at all.

00:02:43.651 --> 00:02:45.875
Reading is separate from managing.

00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:50.489
Manage data connections and Manage connected data sets are for the people who

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:52.101
set the connections up.

00:02:54.101 --> 00:02:58.217
Connected data sets appear next to the site's own data in reports and

00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:01.895
pipelines, and one permission rule decides who can read them.

00:03:01.895 --> 00:03:03.321
Thanks for watching.

